<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>German spy scandal threatens national security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c80866f531f4ce1a89181e7f3160c1ac66da3d775df7eafae81d5b8ab29695b3</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T12:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-spy-scandal-threatens-national-security/a-79580000--1e3ca23b32e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-spy-scandal-threatens-national-security/a-79580000?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of Germany's former intelligence chief August Hanning could undermine national security, experts warn, as allies may reconsider their intelligence relationships.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: UK's Burnham visits Berlin for talks with Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb5a584f875e3be832adefa313334c9e1c1d3deb14bd39ff2d7323da54b20bab</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-uk-s-burnham-visits-berlin-for-talks-with-merz/live-79587637--034eb10b538b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-uk-s-burnham-visits-berlin-for-talks-with-merz/live-79587637?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham is visiting Berlin to launch a new bilateral treaty and hold talks with Chancellor Friedrich Merz. President Steinmeier is on a state visit to France. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa5173df581f4d9780e214fecc9b2c12814f13a792ac1c56c6e61ad168ffb4c5</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz rails against extremism, AfD sympathizers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18cdf673e6b8fbc7bf8fbcbffbed3a1a92f2c018778ebd3c5939ac86b6ff3829</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924--74b91e3a40aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political extremism threatens Germany's existing social order, Chancellor Merz has said. The Transport Ministry has proposed a five-year plan to improve Germany's ailing railroad infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Ex-spy chief sent to pretrial detention on treason charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce837662138885d8112721372b54acaff7d4b784ab8931a30252e69befc4a846</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-ex-spy-chief-sent-to-pretrial-detention-on-treason-charges/a-79576300--68ee19fee871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-ex-spy-chief-sent-to-pretrial-detention-on-treason-charges/a-79576300?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">August Hanning has been remanded into pretrial detention after his arrest. The case has prompted calls for transparency when spies leave the government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German Bundeswehr: A new naval port in Emden aims to enhance Germany's defense capabilities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2620096bc3b41a747599fde206232f6b005e1ddfb3b233b8e80ac7f417331d64</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414--c280e8efd5f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing the escalating security threat, Germany's Navy has decided to establish a second port on the North Sea coast. Emden was chosen as the location.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German politicians warn of antisemitism on October 7 anniversary</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e24befd214d4dafe5a41f42ae04839a4eb5e855ce0c96fb7d80d97e2cef901e3</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-politicians-warn-of-antisemitism-on-october-7-anniversary/a-79583326--969f707c1abe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-politicians-warn-of-antisemitism-on-october-7-anniversary/a-79583326?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leading German politicians including Chancellor Merz and President Steinmeier called for people to reject antisemitism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Did CDU lawmakers support the far-right AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8392ed477d5c1beb3fd7a66bc9737647a7df732909ca9848b1731c6bebf9ab5c</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396--ed4eac4ecf1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lawmakers of the center-right CDU may have voted for the far-right AfD candidate for parliamentary speaker in Saxony-Anhalt. Germany's Social Democrats warn of a "unique breach of taboos."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96a076eebd0cfebe0b10b40d5c83bb02e0fd519327e91102ba41f608af7fa7aa</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284015c9b1a86f144f15794ca2eac524de6d2294466427c76ee4bef612ffccfb</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
